From cd222515ffbc96cf7d3f81422a56019c5a6a617b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:41:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/40] Fix merging of identical functions whose address is
 taken

Backport of 904c0400f093c4d59110497de634d3e0cdfce5bd (branch
fix/dropped-init-fn, on upstream main 4da3147) to v1.32.273.

The Linker.cpp, Linker.h and InterCodeGenerator.cpp hunks apply as they
are (the 0x10000000 bit of LinkerObject::mFlags is free in v1.32.273 as
well).  GlobalAnalyzer::Analyze's EX_TYPECAST case returns the analysed
operand in v1.32.273, where upstream (since 349b10a) returns the cast's
type; the RegisterProc call is added and the v1.32.273 return value is
kept, so nothing else changes.  The autotest.bat entry goes at the top of
the list as upstream.

autotest/funcptrmergetest.c is upstream's test unchanged.  Its last part,
a function k called directly with a constant and then through its
address as an integer, also needs the parameter fix of upstream bf42402
(PR #440, the commit before the r19 backport on this branch): without it
v1.32.273 keeps propagating the constant into k.  The test fails with
v1.32.273 in eight of the ten configurations (-O0 never runs
CombineSameConst) and passes with this change, as does
tools/oscar64-upstream/cases/fn_only_in_global_initializer.c (wrong at
-bc and -n default before).

Linker::CombineSameConst folds linker objects with identical bytes and
references into one, and that includes function code. Two functions
that compile to the same code, e.g. empty stubs or dead stores, were
merged even when the program takes their addresses, so pointers to
different functions compared equal and function pointer tables held
the same entry twice. This happened at every level that enables
COPT_OPTIMIZE_BASIC (-O1 and up, -n and -bc); -O0 was unaffected.

Mark the linker object of a function with DTF_FUNC_VARIABLE (its
address is used as a value) with LOBJF_FUNC_VARIABLE and exclude such
objects from CombineSameConst. Functions that are only called directly
are merged as before.

Two related ways for distinct functions to share an address are closed
as well: a function whose address is only used through a cast to an
integer, (unsigned)f, was never given DTF_FUNC_VARIABLE because
GlobalAnalyzer::Analyze did not register the operand of EX_TYPECAST
(this also made its calling convention differ from an indirect call
through that integer), and Linker::Forwards appended a function that
is a bare JMP to its target, so both ended up at the same address.

Prepared with AI assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J5rsu7nnbQYnRY7GP34gdn
